  "body": "Maintainer direction (2026-11-11): high cohesion, low coupling, because every gate is costly. Put the three rules proposed in the #919 research into AGENTS.md \"Code shape\" and \"Testing\" (which still calls `crates/app/tests/` \"app + commands\"), and name them in the PR-reviewer checklist and the work-issue skill:\n\n1. A test lives with the code it tests: a new test file goes in the lowest crate that provides everything it imports; its Gate map names the real crate.\n2. No new dependency between our crates without a decision entry that lists the imported items, why the caller cannot pass the value in, and what now rebuilds.\n3. `app` holds the document, nothing else: new code goes in `crates/app/src` only if it reads or writes the ECS world, the project file, a command, MCP or the CLI.\n\nThe fourth proposed rule (a new test joins an existing suite) is NOT part of this issue: it waits for directory suites in xtask and for timings. The exact wording of rule 2's small-dependency clause (\"fewer than five items\") is the maintainer's to confirm on the PR.\n\nProcess files: bump `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`; announce on #681 when merged.\n\nDone means: the three rules are in AGENTS.md in plain English, each checkable from a diff; the reviewer agent and the work-issue skill name them.\n\nLists, counts and evidence: the research comment on #919 (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/919#issuecomment-6808141599).\n\nPart of #919.\n",
